Step 3 – Create a Demo User in Cognito
3.1 What are we doing?
    We are creating a student account inside the Cognito User Pool.
    
    Unlike our earlier implementation, where we stored user details and password hashes in DynamoDB, Cognito will manage the user credentials.
    
    Cognito securely stores the password and handles password verification during login.
3.2 Demo user details
    Attribute	Value
    Username	student1
    Email	student1@example.com
    Name	Demo Student
    Password	Student@123

3.3 Create user
    Execute:
    aws cognito-idp admin-create-user \
      --user-pool-id "$POOL_ID" \
      --username student1 \
      --user-attributes \
          Name=email,Value=student1@example.com \
          Name=name,Value="Demo Student" \
          Name=email_verified,Value=true \
      --message-action SUPPRESS \
      --region ap-south-1


      --message-action SUPPRESS prevents Cognito from sending an invitation email.


3.4 Set permanent password
      By default, Cognito creates users with a temporary password when using this command.
      
      We will set a permanent password for our demo user.
      
      Execute:
      aws cognito-idp admin-set-user-password \
        --user-pool-id "$POOL_ID" \
        --username student1 \
        --password 'Student@123' \
        --permanent \
        --region ap-south-1


3.5 Verify user creation
Execute:
      aws cognito-idp admin-get-user \
        --user-pool-id "$POOL_ID" \
        --username student1 \
        --region ap-south-1 \
        --query '{Username:Username,Status:UserStatus,Enabled:Enabled,Attributes:UserAttributes}'
      


