Step 4 – Connect Amazon Cognito with login.html
4.1 Retrieve Cognito Configuration
    What are we doing?
    Our frontend needs two important identifiers to communicate with Cognito:
    1. User Pool ID: Identifies the Cognito user directory.
    2. App Client ID: Identifies our web application.
    We will retrieve both automatically and save them into shell variables.
4.1.1 – Retrieve User Pool ID
      Execute:
      POOL_ID=$(aws cognito-idp list-user-pools \
        --max-results 60 \
        --region ap-south-1 \
        --query "UserPools[?Name=='day2-auth-user-pool'].Id | [0]" \
        --output text)
      
      echo "User Pool ID: $POOL_ID"


4.1.2 – Retrieve App Client ID
      CLIENT_ID=$(aws cognito-idp list-user-pool-clients \
        --user-pool-id "$POOL_ID" \
        --region ap-south-1 \
        --query "UserPoolClients[?ClientName=='day2-auth-web-client'].ClientId | [0]" \
        --output text)
      
      echo "App Client ID: $CLIENT_ID"


4.1.3 – Capture AWS Region
    AWS_REGION="ap-south-1"

====================
Step 4.2 – Integrate login.html with Amazon Cognito
      4.2.1 What are we doing?
      We will replace the existing custom authentication logic in login.html with direct Amazon Cognito authentication.
      
      Previously:
      
      login.html → API Gateway → Lambda → DynamoDB
      
      Now:
      
      login.html → Amazon Cognito User Pool
      
      The browser will communicate directly with Cognito using its App Client ID.
      
      We will use the Cognito InitiateAuth API with the USER_PASSWORD_AUTH flow.

What happens during login?
      1. Student enters username and password.
      2. JavaScript sends credentials to Cognito.
      3. Cognito validates the credentials.
      4. Cognito returns authentication tokens.
      5. Browser stores the tokens in session storage.
      6. Browser redirects to Dashboard.html.
      No Lambda, API Gateway or external JavaScript library is needed for this implementation.
4.2.2 Replace login.html
    Execute this complete command: ( You already have created frontend folder . execute it there if possible)
   

cat > login.html <<'HTML'
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Student Login - Cognito</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #eef2f7;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            min-height: 100vh;
            margin: 0;
        }

        .login-container {
            background: white;
            padding: 35px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            width: 340px;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }

        h2 {
            text-align: center;
            color: #1e3a5f;
        }

        input {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 12px;
            margin: 10px 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            border-radius: 6px;
        }

        button {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 12px;
            margin-top: 15px;
            background: #2563eb;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 6px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
        }

        button:disabled {
            background: #888;
            cursor: not-allowed;
        }

        #message {
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 15px;
            color: red;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="login-container">
    <h2>Student Login</h2>

    <form id="loginForm">
        <input
            type="text"
            id="username"
            placeholder="Username"
            autocomplete="username"
            required
        >

        <input
            type="password"
            id="password"
            placeholder="Password"
            autocomplete="current-password"
            required
        >

        <button type="submit" id="loginButton">Login</button>
    </form>

    <div id="message"></div>
</div>

<script>

const REGION = "ap-south-1";
const CLIENT_ID = "REPLACE_WITH_APP_CLIENT_ID";

const COGNITO_URL =
    `https://cognito-idp.${REGION}.amazonaws.com/`;

document.getElementById("loginForm")
.addEventListener("submit", async function(event) {

    event.preventDefault();

    const username =
        document.getElementById("username").value.trim();

    const password =
        document.getElementById("password").value;

    const message =
        document.getElementById("message");

    const button =
        document.getElementById("loginButton");

    button.disabled = true;
    button.textContent = "Authenticating...";
    message.textContent = "";

    try {

        const response = await fetch(COGNITO_URL, {
            method: "POST",
            headers: {
                "Content-Type": "application/x-amz-json-1.1",
                "X-Amz-Target":
                    "AWSCognitoIdentityProviderService.InitiateAuth"
            },
            body: JSON.stringify({
                AuthFlow: "USER_PASSWORD_AUTH",
                ClientId: CLIENT_ID,
                AuthParameters: {
                    USERNAME: username,
                    PASSWORD: password
                }
            })
        });

        const data = await response.json();

        if (
            response.ok &&
            data.AuthenticationResult
        ) {

            sessionStorage.setItem(
                "cognito_tokens",
                JSON.stringify(data.AuthenticationResult)
            );

            sessionStorage.setItem(
                "cognito_username",
                username
            );

            window.location.href = "Dashboard.html";

        } else {

            window.location.href = "Login_failure.html";

        }

    } catch (error) {

        message.textContent =
            "Unable to connect to authentication service.";

        button.disabled = false;
        button.textContent = "Login";

    }

});

</script>

</body>
</html>
