Step 4.4 – Upload Updated Frontend Files to S3
4.4.1 What are we doing?
      We have modified:
      - login.html – Now authenticates directly with Amazon Cognito.
      - Dashboard.html – Displays information from Cognito's ID Token.
      We need to upload these updated files to S3 so CloudFront can serve the new application.
4.4.2 Upload updated files
      We will use your existing S3 bucket stored in $BUCKET.
      
      Execute:
      
      aws s3 cp login.html s3://$BUCKET/login.html \
        --content-type "text/html"
      
      aws s3 cp Dashboard.html s3://$BUCKET/Dashboard.html \
        --content-type "text/html"

We need to invalidate the Cloudfront Cache. But since we have already configured a event driven invalidation for our cloudfront., it will be automatic





















